okf_version: "1.0"
task: "User: need to be able to restart the LLM CLI runtime I am currently using with --continue, through the ciel router; and the command must be visible over MCP so it can be sent from outside or let the agent restart itself."
problem: "The router and the CLI client are separate processes. Only the launcher (ciel-runtime cli) owns the CLI child process, its console and its exact argv/env, so a router-side tool cannot relaunch the session by itself. The router MCP server also was not attached to sessions unless the web backend + LLM channel delivery were both on, so an agent had no way to call such a tool."
design:
  request_file: "Single-slot JSON file in the router instance directory (shared through CIEL_RUNTIME_STATE_DIR): runtime-session-restart.json, schema ciel-runtime.runtime-session-restart/v1, fields id/source/reason/runtime/target_pid/resume/requested_at/expires_at. TTL default 300s; an expired or corrupt slot is dropped with a log."
  client_supervisor: "The CLI transports poll the slot while the CLI child runs: the Windows ConPTY proxy loop, the POSIX PTY proxy loop, and the direct Popen path (channel_terminal_dispatch._await_child). On a matching request they terminate the child and record the request in a process-local control (RuntimeSessionRestartControl)."
  relaunch: "run_claude/run_codex wrap the transport in a restart loop: on a claimed request the CLI is relaunched with the runtime's session-continue argument (claude --continue, codex resume --last) unless the argv already selects a session (--continue/--resume/-c/--session-id/--fork-session/--from-pr for Claude Code; a resume subcommand or a real --continue for Codex, where -c key=value is a config override). Repeat request ids are ignored so an unclearable slot cannot loop the relaunch."
  targets: "The queue resolves the newest live client of the instance (router-clients/*.json, pid liveness checked) or an explicit client pid. A request targets that launcher pid; target_pid=0 means any client."
  surfaces: "MCP tool restart_session on the ciel-runtime-router server (/ca/mcp) and the CLI command ciel-runtime restart-session [--pid N|--workspace PATH] [--runtime NAME] [--reason TEXT] [--no-resume] (runtimes: ciel-runtime ... and ciel-runtimectl restart-session)."
  mcp_attachment: "Routed launches now attach the router MCP server by default (claude_code.router_mcp=false restores the old behavior, native Anthropic/Codex launches keep the old behavior). Without this the session has no restart_session tool, so the agent could not restart itself."
scope: "claude and codex CLI launches carry the relaunch loop. codex-app-server/agy/grok/zcode/muse do not: a request for them expires unclaimed with a log entry."
safety: "RuntimeSessionRestartService.queue refuses to run from an unisolated test process (test_isolation_guard.unisolated_test_process), the same fail-closed rule the router/client termination paths use."
verification:
  probe: "scripts/probe_runtime_session_restart.py, CIEL_RUNTIME_TEST_ISOLATED=1, RESULT: OK. dispatch (ConPTY console proxy) and direct transports: a request for this pid was queued, claimed by the client, the 120s child was terminated after 1.2s (returncode 1), the request file was consumed, and the relaunch argv ended with --continue."
  probe_mcp: "An isolated router on a scratch config/instance directory advertised 7 tools including restart_session; a tools/call restart_session returned ok/queued with the resolved target pid and wrote runtime-session-restart.json. is_error=false."
  launcher_loop: "tests/test_runtime_session_restart.py drives the real run_claude loop with a stubbed transport: first child argv has no --continue, the second (after the request) ends with --continue; a launch without a request runs once."
  tests: "run_test_group unit/router/channel/runtime all OK (1487/1133/406/296)."
live_state: "The live routers 9611 (Claude Code) and 9465 (Codex) still advertise the old 6 MCP tools because they run the pre-change build; they pick up restart_session when the session is relaunched. The 9465/codex session exited during this work (pid 89280/59512 gone) - not through this code path, which only touches its own instance directory and its own child processes."
not_done: "No version bump, no deploy. Reasoning-streaming on the translated Responses route remains the open item from before."
